<section class="detail-panel">
    <p class="muted">Last updated: 29 September 2026</p>
    <h2>How we review job listings</h2>
    <p>D2DJobs organizes opportunities from employer career pages, official recruitment notices, recruiters, and employer submissions. Before a listing qualifies for search indexing or advertising, our publishing checks require a company, role, location, qualification, skills, description, eligibility, selection process, application link, official source, and last-verified date.</p>

    <h2>What we add</h2>
    <p>We structure the practical facts candidates need to compare opportunities: eligibility, experience, location, relevant skills, closing dates, selection steps, and how to apply. We link to the source so readers can verify the opening and complete the application with the employer. We do not present copied third-party material as our own reporting.</p>

    <h2>Incomplete or changing information</h2>
    <p>A listing that does not meet the publishing checks is marked as needing verification, excluded from the sitemap, set to noindex, and does not display programmatic advertising. Openings can change without notice, so candidates should always confirm the details on the linked source before applying.</p>

    <h2>Employer submissions and paid placement</h2>
    <p>Employer-submitted jobs require administrative review before publication. Featured placement is clearly labelled and affects presentation only; payment does not guarantee publication or change our review standard. Browsing and applying remain free for job seekers.</p>

    <h2>Corrections and expired listings</h2>
    <p>Listings with supplied closing dates stop appearing after expiry. If you find a closed role, broken link, incorrect requirement, or misleading detail, email <a href="mailto:contactsupport21@gmail.com?subject=D2DJobs%20listing%20correction">contactsupport21@gmail.com</a> with the listing URL and the correction. We will review the source and update, pause, or remove the listing as appropriate.</p>

    <h2>Editorial responsibility</h2>
    <p>D2DJobs is operated by Subash.G. Questions about these standards can be sent through the <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Contact">Contact page</a>.</p>
</section>
